       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release), and the largest single dose is typically 850 to 1,000 mg. This dose is twice the maximum, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO** at some other frequency\n\nTell me which one you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is intended. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note that you verified the dose."
